Z||000000||fotofrank||04-13-2001||06:20 PM||||I have an '84 Iron Duke. I added the rally gauges and an oil pressure sensor from a V6. <BR>With the oil sensor connected as stock '84 the 12volt from the battery drains to ground through the sensor. i change the source of the 12Volts to the ignition 12volts to the distributor. Now I can not turn the car off. that is it keeps running with the key out and ignition switch in the "locked position" What now?<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-13-2001||06:27 PM||||You'll need to yank the coil wire to kill it. Put a heavy CLEAN DRY Glove on, or use a stick or something so you don't get zapped.<P>Then disconect the battery.<P>2 posibilities... <P>you wired something wrong on the new gauge or the sender. I don't just know how but it's posible.<P>check the linkage between the ignition switch and lock. You'll need to drop the column. The linkage may have picked now to break. (This is a common problem in tilt column but non tilt can do it to.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fotofrank||04-13-2001||11:18 PM||||More wierdness....with the ignition on , car running and I push the rear deck remote releas the rear deck opens. With the ignition off, in the locked position and I push he deck remote release the car turns off.<BR>My ques is that with the ignition off the 12volts is back feeding to the ignition and fuel pump! <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||1
